/**
 * @mainpage ft_nm
 *
 * A C implementation of the @c nm command: list the symbols of ELF files
 * (32 and 64 bits, little endian) and of ar archives.
 *
 * @section usage Usage
 *
 * @code
 * ./ft_nm [-a] [-g] [-p] [-r] [-u] [-h] [file...]
 * @endcode
 *
 * Without file, @c a.out is read. See nm_args for the options.
 *
 * @section flow Program flow
 *
 * -# init() runs before main(): registers the program name and starts the
 *    resource collector.
 * -# get_options() parses the command line into #options.
 * -# mainloop() opens and maps each file (file_manip.h), then hands it to
 *    display_ar_file() or display_elf_file().
 * -# is_elf_format() checks the file, read_elfN() extracts the symbols and
 *    get_symbol_type() deduces their letter.
 * -# print_symbols() sorts, filters and prints them.
 *
 * @section modules Modules
 *
 * | Header               | Role                                        |
 * |----------------------|---------------------------------------------|
 * | nm_elf.h             | ELF types, checks and symbol extraction     |
 * | nm_ar.h              | ar archive constants and helpers            |
 * | print.h              | Symbol output and error messages            |
 * | options.h            | Command line options                        |
 * | file_manip.h         | Opening and mapping of the input files      |
 * | resource_collector.h | Release of all resources at exit            |
 * | xalloc.h             | Allocation wrappers that exit on failure    |
 */
